WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.988
Learn to develop and apply a formula for determining perimeter of square and

00:00:04.988 --> 00:00:09.408
rectangle and construct different rectangles for a given perimeter (cm, m) to

00:00:09.408 --> 00:00:12.723
demonstrate that many shapes are possible for a perimeter

00:00:13.533 --> 00:00:20.438
Calculate the perimeter of a 7 m long, 10 m wide school garden. The answer is 34 m. P

00:00:20.438 --> 00:00:23.709
equals 2 times (7 plus 10) equals 34 m.

00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:30.175
A rectangular school garden measures 15 m by 4 m. How much fencing is needed for all

00:00:30.175 --> 00:00:33.493
four sides? Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:39.487
The answer is 38 m. 2 times (15 plus 4) equals 38 m.
